# Rules of the environment-variable schema. Read by lib/core/envschema.sh; the variables themselves (key, file, type, default,
# description) come from the glossary lib/help/variables.txt, so a variable added there shows up in the schema without touching this file.
# Here only what a glossary line cannot say: how to validate a value and whether it is a secret.
#
# One rule per line, "pattern|validator|secret", the FIRST rule that matches wins:
#   pattern    a glob on the key (`*_PORT`), or `<file>:<glob>` to limit it to one file (`.env.s1:IP_INTERNAL_CONNECTION`)
#   validator  the check of the value (functions ev_<name> of envschema.sh; list in docs/env-variables.md): text, port, mongo-uri,
#              public-url, url, url-ws, b64-32, secret-path, memory, bool, services-list, instance-name, image-name, tag, int,
#              secret-min32, host, registry, duration, json-line, path
#   secret     1 when the value is a secret: it is masked when listed and never printed unless asked for (0 otherwise)
# Which variables the tool can GENERATE comes from the service catalog (lib/core/catalog.data, last field), not from here.
.env.instance:INSTANCE|instance-name|0
.env.instance:REGISTRY|registry|0
.env.instance:COMPOSE_PROFILES|services-list|0
.env.instance:DATA_DIR|path|0
IP_SERVER|public-url|0
AUTH_URL|url|0
TRANSCRIPTOR_URL|url|0
LIVEKIT_URL|url-ws|0
MONGO*URI|mongo-uri|1
JWT_EXPIRES_IN|duration|0
DELTA_UNIVERSITY_HANDOFF_SECRET|secret-min32|1
FEDERATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY|b64-32|1
FCM_CERT|secret-path|0
*_FCM_CERT|secret-path|0
SERVERS_CONFIG|json-line|1
IP_INTERNAL_CONNECTION|host|0
TCP_LISTEN_HOST|host|0
*_PORT|port|0
PORT_*|port|0
*_TAG|tag|0
*_IMAGE|image-name|0
*_MEM_LIMIT|memory|0
*_ENABLED|bool|0
*_CONCURRENCY|int|0
*_SECONDS|int|0
*_DIR|path|0
API_KEY_*|text|1
*_API_KEY|text|1
*_SECRET|text|1
*_KEY|text|1
*_TOKEN|text|1
*SECRET*|text|1
*TOKEN*|text|1
*PASS*|text|1
*PWD*|text|1
*CREDENTIAL*|text|1
*PRIVATE*|text|1
*_URI|text|1
*_URL|url|0
*|text|0
